+# aims Guide State
+
+Loop status only. Not the design record.
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** A Session-level default timeout whose resolution (call value vs session default) has exactly
+one owner that every request path through the session funnels through (request(), direct send(), every
+redirect hop, a hook/auth re-send), while a Session with no default behaves bit-for-bit as today.
+
+**Why now:** Product change received: a per-Session default timeout that every request made through the session uses unless the call passes its own.
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [x] C0 characterization first: Session with no default hands the adapter timeout=None on get, direct send, redirect hop.
+- [x] C1 s.timeout=5; s.get(u) -> adapter gets 5.
+- [x] C2 s.timeout=5; s.get(u, timeout=2) -> 2.
+- [x] C3 s.timeout=(3,30); timeout=5 -> 5 (wholesale replacement); s.timeout=5; timeout=(1,None) -> (1,None).
+- [x] C4 falsifier: s.timeout=5; s.get(u, timeout=None) -> 5, NOT None (the "None = forever" shortcut fails this).
+- [x] C5 s.send(prep) without timeout -> default; s.send(prep, timeout=1) -> 1.
+- [x] C6 every redirect hop uses the same resolved timeout (default and per-call override).
+- [x] C7 response hooks get the resolved timeout in kwargs (digest auth re-sends via r.connection.send(prep, **kwargs), auth.py:312).
+- [x] C8 pickle keeps s.timeout; unpickling pre-feature state (no timeout key) -> working session, no default.
+- [x] C9 module-level requests.get unchanged; urllib3 Timeout object accepted as default.
+- [x] Full suite: only the 4 known TestTimeout connect failures.
+
+**Preserve:**
+- A Session with no default configured behaves exactly as today (no timeout unless the call passes one).
+- Module-level `requests.get(...)` etc. behave exactly as today.
+- An explicit numeric / tuple / urllib3 Timeout per call behaves exactly as today.
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- A timeout value type / validation layer (Session settings are plain attributes; invalid values already fail fast in HTTPAdapter.send).
+- Per-host / per-method timeouts; env-var timeouts.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+ROLE: implementation Worker. DESIGN GOAL: the session default timeout is one setting with one resolution
+owner every path through the Session uses; no path re-derives or bypasses it. BEHAVIOR: C0-C9; rule chosen:
+omitted or None per-call timeout -> session default; any concrete per-call value replaces it wholesale.
+GOOD: design-principles.md + add-feature-principles.md; match requests' grain (plain attributes, __attrs__,
+merge_setting). TESTING: characterization first, then test-first per criterion, recording adapter, no network.
+RETURN: code + tests + where the rule lives; met|partially_met|invalidated|blocked.
+(No subagent facility in this host: executed as a separate phase.)
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- 
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] Resolved: explicit timeout=None -> session default (PO delegated the choice; Guide chose).
+- [x] File decision + rejected alternative in src/requests/sessions.py.md; anchor it.
+- [x] User docs (advanced.rst timeouts + sessions) and HISTORY.md reflect the new rule.
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met — tests/test_session_timeout.py (29 tests) covers C0-C9, and C0 passed before the change. Full suite:
+644 passed, only the 4 known TestTimeout connect failures remain. The rule has one owner (Session.send,
+one merge_setting line). The decision is filed in src/requests/sessions.py.md (anchored).
+
