diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..55d0e7e 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,22 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+A :class:`Session <requests.Session>` can carry a default timeout, used by
+every request sent through it that does not pass its own::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)  # uses 60 for this request only
+
+A request's own timeout replaces the session default entirely; a single value
+is not merged into a default tuple. On a session with a default, passing
+``timeout=None`` also uses the default, so a request made through that session
+cannot wait forever; pass a larger value if one request needs longer. The
+default applies to redirects and to :meth:`Session.send
+<requests.Session.send>` as well.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
